import Contracts.Track.Reach.LegTube

/-!
# The leg theorem: the certified gains of the reference directions (generated by `gen_lean_A.py`)

REACH.md §9. The fields of `RefGains` (LegTube.lean), certified. The direction gains are the
per-coordinate gains of the **transposed** models: `resp Aᵀ D m j = (Aᵐ D)ⱼ = rsp A eⱼ D m`
(`resp_transpose`), so `Nominal.gain_assemble` (the machinery of `GainH.out*`, `GainV.out*`) applied
to `Âᵀ` with the initial vector `S · D` gives `Σₘ |(Aᵐ D)ⱼ|` for every coordinate `j`: forward
trajectories of `B_h` and of the acceleration shift `vAcc` (4096 ticks, Neumann tail with
`|A_h^2048| ≤ Mnᵀ`) and `B_v` (2048 ticks, `|A_v^1024| ≤ Mnᵀ`), checked by the kernel in chunks of
32 ticks. The jerk gain of the command rate is the `c₁` gain of `B_h` (`rate_shift`); the jerk gain
of the command `c₁` is the `c₁` coordinate of the `vAcc` trajectory. The tails past `Mc = 416` and
`Mt = 1728` ticks are the certified states `A^{416} D`, `A^{1728} D` (`round_err` at the
checkpoints 13 and 54) weighted by the certified per-coordinate ℓ1 gains `GH 0`, `GV 0`
(`tail_of_state`) or, for the velocity defect `e₁`, by the peak gains `PH 0` (`peak_of_state`).
-/

